//? Title: Heapsort: build a heap, grow a sorted suffix
//? Subtitle: Actual sift exchanges, linear heap construction and explicit history storage
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Rearrange an integer array into ascending order without allocating a second
array for the in-place sorting algorithm. A binary max-heap makes the largest
remaining value easy to select, but every extraction must repair the smaller
active heap. This report follows actual build and extraction swaps, retains the
original six-value example, and checks a linear bound on heap construction. It
separates worst-case sort work from easy equal-value cases, and distinguishes
the legacy constant-space sorter from owned run results and potentially
quadratic full-state histories.
)

\toc

> A three-value repair before the full example

For input 1,3,2, bottom-up construction repairs index 0. The left child 3
becomes the candidate; the right child 2 does not exceed it. One actual swap
gives 3,1,2. There are two strict key comparisons and one build swap. The
following program reads the completed build snapshot and the actual exchange
records from a single shared heapsort execution.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/heapsort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::heapsort_trace({1, 3, 2});
    const auto &heap = t.states.at(1).data;
    std::print("| phase enum | heap size at swap | left | right | left before | right before | root parking " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.swaps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", int(e.phase),
                   e.heap_size, e.left, e.right, e.left_before, e.right_before,
                   e.root_parking);
    std::print("\nBuilt heap {} {} {}; actual build key comparisons {}; build sift swaps {}.\n",
               heap[0], heap[1], heap[2], t.run.build.key_comparisons,
               t.run.build.sift_swaps);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d(90, 1000);
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;
    style.circle = true;
    style.width = 1.2;
    style.height = 1.2;
    style.font_size = 23;
    const std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> positions{{2, 2}, {0, 0},
                                                            {4, 0}};
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 3; ++i)
        d.node(std::to_string(i), positions[i],
               std::format("i{}\n{}", i, heap[i]), style);
    d.edge("0", "1").edge("0", "2").text({2, 4},
                                         "Actual build: [1,3,2] → [3,1,2]", 26).text({2, -1.5}, "Children of i: 2i+1 and 2i+2", 23).save_svg("build/heapsort_tiny.svg");
    if (heap != std::vector<std::int64_t>{3, 1, 2} ||
        t.run.build.key_comparisons != 2)
        throw std::runtime_error("tiny repair");
}
```
