\caption(The native concept diagram uses the producing completed-build snapshot. Build and extraction events are separated by phase; enum values are Build 1 and Extract 2.)
\alttext(A three-node tree places 3 at root index 0,1 at child index 1 and 2 at child index 2, after one actual bottom-up repair.)

> Why the implicit tree can be repaired

Number the complete binary tree by array indices starting at zero. Children of i
are 2i+1 and 2i+2 when present; the parent of a nonroot node is ⌊(i−1)/2⌋.
Internal nodes have i<n/2, so child arithmetic is performed only after that safe
bound check. The max-heap property is

$$A_i\ge A_{2i+1},\qquad A_i\ge A_{2i+2}\quad\text{for existing children}.$$
\alttext(Each parent dominates its existing children, making the root a maximum of the active prefix.)

Sift-down assumes both child subtrees are already heaps. It compares the parent
candidate with the left child, then with the right child if present. If the
candidate remains the parent it stops; otherwise it swaps with the strict larger
candidate and descends. A tie never replaces the current candidate. Swapping
restores the relation above the next visited node, and only the moved value may
still violate its new children. A downward path is finite and has at most the
subtree's height in exchanges, proving termination and repair correctness.

Bottom-up construction visits internal roots from n/2−1 down to 0. Their child
subtrees have already been repaired. Induction gives a heap at completion,
without assuming the whole input was initially a heap.

> The original six values: heap prefix and sorted suffix

The original array is 3,7,1,9,2,8. Actual build repairs indices 2,1,0 and
produces 9,7,8,3,2,1. Each extraction parks the heap root at its last active
position, reduces the heap size, then repairs the remaining prefix. The table
and figure below contain the input, completed build and every completed
extraction from one execution. Blue denotes the active prefix and green the
sorted suffix; numbers remain actual integer values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/heapsort_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const std::vector<std::int64_t> input{3, 7, 1, 9, 2, 8};
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::heapsort_trace(input);
    std::vector<double> hx, hy, sx, sy;
    std::print("| checkpoint | phase enum | heap size | full actual array | swaps so far |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < t.states.size(); ++j) {
        const auto &s = t.states[j];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |", j, int(s.phase), s.heap_size);
        for (auto x : s.data)
            std::print(" {}", x);
        std::print(" | {} |\n", s.swaps_done);
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.data.size(); ++i) {
            auto &x = i < s.heap_size ? hx : sx;
            auto &y = i < s.heap_size ? hy : sy;
            x.push_back(i);
            y.push_back(-double(j));
        }
    }
    std::print("\nFinal sorted output:");
    for (auto x : t.run.data)
        std::print(" {}", x);
    std::print(". Build comparisons {}; extraction comparisons {}; root parking swaps {}.\n",
               t.run.build.key_comparisons, t.run.extraction.key_comparisons,
               t.run.extraction.root_swaps);
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    plot.points(hx, hy, "active heap/input", {37, 99, 235}, 17.).points(
        sx, sy, "sorted suffix", {5, 150, 105}, 17.);
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < t.states.size(); ++j)
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 6; ++i)
            plot.text(i, -double(j), std::to_string(t.states[j].data[i]),
                      {255, 255, 255}, 14.);
    plot.title("Original array: each extraction grows the sorted suffix").x_label("zero-based array index").y_label("negative checkpoint index: input, build, then repairs").x_limits(-.5, 5.5).y_limits(-7, 2).save_svg("build/heapsort_original.svg");
    auto expected = input;
    std::sort(expected.begin(), expected.end());
    if (t.run.data != expected ||
        t.states[1].data != std::vector<std::int64_t>{9, 7, 8, 3, 2, 1})
        throw std::runtime_error("original output");
}
