Final sorted output: 1 2 3 7 8 9. Build comparisons 7; extraction comparisons 8; root parking swaps 5.
\image(figures/heapsort_original.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Every post-build checkpoint has a max-heap prefix and an ascending suffix. The initial blue array need not be a heap. Input 0, Build 1 and Extract 2 identify the phase.)
\alttext(Seven rows show the original six values, their built heap and five completed extractions, with the sorted suffix growing from the right.)

The sorting invariant is: the prefix is a max-heap, the suffix is ascending, and
every suffix value is at least every prefix value. Root parking extends that
suffix by its smallest new member; repair preserves the remaining multiset and
heap condition. After n−1 extractions only one prefix value remains, so the full
array is ascending. No key arithmetic is used, permitting the entire int64
range.

> Prove and check linear construction

At least h levels can lie below exactly ⌊n/2^h⌋ nodes in a complete binary heap.
Counting each node once per level of its height gives the exact height sum

$$H(n)=\sum_{h\ge1}\left\lfloor\frac{n}{2^h}\right\rfloor=n-\operatorname{popcount}(n)<n\quad(n>0).$$
\alttext(The sum of subtree heights equals n minus the number of one bits in n, which is strictly less than n for nonempty input.)

A sift from height h applies at most h downward swaps and at most 2h key
comparisons. Therefore build sift swaps are at most H(n) and build comparisons
at most 2H(n). There are n/2 sift calls; terminal leaf checks do not compare
keys. This avoids the old ceiling-series argument, which discarded rounding
terms without justification.

For sorting, each of n−1 reduced-prefix repairs traverses at most ⌊log2 n⌋
levels, giving an O(n log n) worst-case upper bound. This is not a claim that
every input takes Θ(n log n). The equal-valued family stops every sift
immediately and needs only linear selected comparisons, though root parking
still swaps n−1 times.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/heapsort_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::vector<double> x, build, extract, equal;
    std::print("| n | ascending build comparisons | 2H(n) | ascending extraction comparisons | equal " "extraction comparisons |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (unsigned power = 1; power <= 12; ++power) {
        const std::size_t n = std::size_t{1} << power;
        std::vector<std::int64_t> ascending(n);
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i)
            ascending[i] = i;
        const auto a = dm::algorithms::heapsort_run(ascending);
        const auto e =
            dm::algorithms::heapsort_run(std::vector<std::int64_t>(n, 7));
        const auto bound = 2 * (n - std::popcount(n));
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, a.build.key_comparisons,
                   bound, a.extraction.key_comparisons,
                   e.extraction.key_comparisons);
        if (a.build.key_comparisons > bound || e.extraction.sift_swaps != 0 ||
            !std::is_sorted(a.data.begin(), a.data.end()))
            throw std::runtime_error("work bound");
        x.push_back(power);
        build.push_back(double(a.build.key_comparisons) / n);
        extract.push_back(double(a.extraction.key_comparisons) / n);
        equal.push_back(double(e.extraction.key_comparisons) / n);
    }
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    plot.line(x, build, "ascending build", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).line(
        x, extract, "ascending extraction", {220, 38, 38}, 2.).line(
        x, equal, "equal extraction", {5, 150, 105}, 2.).title(
        "Actual key comparisons per input value").x_label("log2 n").y_label(
        "selected key comparisons / n").y_limits(0, 30).save_svg(
        "build/heapsort_work.svg");
}
```
