\caption(All curves use actual producing comparison counts; input/output copying, snapshots and allocation are excluded. Constant build ratios agree with the linear bound, while the ascending extraction ratio grows.)
\alttext(Build and equal-value extraction comparisons per value remain bounded near two, while ascending extraction comparisons per value increase with log2 input size.)

> Constant algorithmic space versus owned histories

The in-place `build_max_heap` and `heapsort` entry points allocate nothing, use
iterative repairs and constant auxiliary state. The owned `heapsort_run` first
copies input, adding O(n) working/output storage. The full trace goes further:
it always stores input and completed-build states, even for empty or singleton
inputs, and then n−1 post-repair states for n≥1. If m=2+max(n−1,0), known
snapshot capture is m(n+1) logical units: one record plus n integer values per
state. Each actual swap adds one further unit online.

The default input cap and logical capture cap are each one million, zero
disabling that policy. Known snapshot requirements are checked before working
allocation/copy. Complete snapshot space is reserved in the logical budget,
while each unknown swap record is admitted before that exchange. Fields,
ordinary output, vector capacities and allocation overhead are excluded: these
limits are not byte or peak-RAM bounds. Failure returns no partial history and
leaves the caller's input unchanged. Full-state storage is O(n²), plus O(n log
n) swap records, so the traced variant does not inherit the in-place sorter's
constant-space claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/heapsort_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const std::vector<std::vector<std::int64_t>> inputs{{}, {7}, {2, 2}, {2, 1}};
    std::vector<double> x, snapshots, events;
    std::print("| case | n | snapshots | actual swap events | logical capture units |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < inputs.size(); ++i) {
        const auto t = dm::algorithms::heapsort_trace(inputs[i]);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i + 1, inputs[i].size(),
                   t.states.size(), t.swaps.size(), t.captured_entries);
        x.push_back(i + 1);
        snapshots.push_back(t.states.size() * (inputs[i].size() + 1));
        events.push_back(t.swaps.size());
    }
    const auto tied = dm::algorithms::heapsort_trace({2, 2});
    const auto &e = tied.swaps.at(0);
    std::print("\nEqual-valued actual exchange: indices {},{}; before-values {},{}; root parking {}.\n",
               e.left, e.right, e.left_before, e.right_before, e.root_parking);
    bool known = false, online = false, inputcap = false;
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::heapsort_trace({2, 1}, {2, 8});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        known = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::heapsort_trace({2, 1}, {2, 9});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        online = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::heapsort_trace({2, 1}, {1, 100});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        inputcap = true;
    }
    const auto exact = dm::algorithms::heapsort_trace({2, 1}, {2, 10});
    std::print("Known snapshot cap8 rejects {}; reserved9 plus first online event rejects {}; input cap1 " "rejects {}; exact10 retains {} units.\n",
               known, online, inputcap, exact.captured_entries);
    if (!known || !online || !inputcap || e.left_before != e.right_before)
        throw std::runtime_error("capture controls");
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    auto left = x, right = x;
    for (auto &v : left)
        v -= .18;
    for (auto &v : right)
        v += .18;
    plot.bars(left, snapshots, "known snapshot units", {37, 99, 235}, .32).bars(
        right, events, "online swap units", {220, 38, 38}, .32).title(
        "Trace storage is distinct from algorithmic auxiliary space").x_label(
        "case: 1 empty; 2 singleton; 3 (2,2); 4 (2,1)").y_label(
        "logical capture units").y_limits(0, 13).save_svg(
        "build/heapsort_controls.svg");
}
```
